WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.950
First, launch Copilot.

00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:05.050
Loading is sped up.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:10.625
Type slash autopilot, followed by your goal.

00:00:10.625 --> 00:00:14.613
Here: fix all TypeScript errors in the source folder.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:21.200
Copilot first asks which permission mode to use.

00:00:21.612 --> 00:00:25.362
We choose Allow All, so it can work uninterrupted.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:29.013
Copilot is now locked onto the goal.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:36.400
It defines what success looks like: zero TypeScript errors, with the build and lint passing.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:43.313
Then it inspects the project: the git status, the TypeScript config, and the source files.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:48.150
And it keeps going until the objective is met.

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:51.512
Think of it like setting a GPS destination.
